    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1350" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aerūgĭno</span></b> , avi, atum,
		1, v. n.
		aerugo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to become rusty</i>, <i>cankered</i> (eccl.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aurum et argentum vestrum aeruginavit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Jac. 5, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sicut aeramentum, aeruginat nequitia illius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Eccli. 12, 10</span></i>
			.</div>
